<title>USA: Winds buffet Iowa corn crop but harvest pace good.</title>
<headline>Winds buffet Iowa corn crop but harvest pace good.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES, Iowa 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Very high winds produced some damage from lodging and ear loss in the Iowa corn crop,  but good progress was made despite the adverse weather, Iowa's Agricultural Statistics Service said.</p>
<p>During the week ended Sunday, corn was 62 percent harvested, against 85 percent last year and 71 percent for the five-year average.</p>
<p>As of Friday, the corn crop condition was rated one percent very poor, three percent poor, 15 percent fair and 81 percent good to excellent.</p>
<p>Thge soybean crop was 96 percent harvested, compared to the average of 99 percent and 99 percent last year, the report said.</p>
<p>Winter wheat planting was 96 percent complete as of Sunday, slightly behind the five-year average of 97 percent.</p>
<p>Soil moisture was rated, 5 percent short, 84 percent adequate and 11 percent surplus.</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8720</p>
</text>
